SUMMARY:Shruti Samvaad
DESCRIPTION:A morning of swar and naad\, where sound becomes a dialogue between artist and audience. \nDr. Shruti Jauhari\, distinguished Hindustani classical vocalist\, scholar\, and educator\, leads this musical performance\, accompanied by Ajay Kulkarni on tabla and Tejas Katoti on harmonium. Beginning with the slow and improvisational Khayal\, they move into Thumri\, its lighter\, more expressive counterpart centred in romance and devotion. The performance is an invitation to share in the rich experience of these musical traditions. The session closes with a samvaad\, an interactive session between the audience and the artists \nSupported by: \n \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nA Hindustani Recital of Morning Ragas\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdNrDaVYO-hkMvbE5iylTXEYmZQoj7j3tWUVVNM5VdcDLc6Ng/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Performers*: Shruti Jauhari \, Ajay Kulkarni\, Tejas Katoti\n*Event Categories*: Music\, Performing Arts
